# .npmignore, once present, replaces .gitignore for `npm pack`/`publish`
# purposes rather than merging with it — so patterns already covered by
# .gitignore (like __pycache__/*.pyc, generated whenever
# templates/hermes/keel_plugin.py is imported/compiled by a test) still
# need to be repeated here, or a locally-generated, Python-version-specific
# bytecode cache file can leak into a published tarball. Confirmed via a
# real `npm publish --dry-run` — see session/v1/EVIDENCE/m5-release.md.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
